Z||000031||Ken Wittlief||07-09-2001||10:39 AM||||I know something that needs to be fixed.<P>whenever I access a subject using Microsoft Internet explorer I have to refresh the page by clicking on the refresh icon - otherwise the page only displays what was there the last time I looked at it.<P>  I have Explorer set up to refresh pages everytime I look at them - and it works for other message boards - for some reason it cant tell these pages have been added to  - only seems to happen on this forum.<P>EDIT: no wait - in typical microsoft fashion I just found a SECOND place to setup the 'refresh on every visit' option - so I will let you know if that fixes this problem.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000032||Steve Normington||07-09-2001||11:09 AM||||More things to do if you're bored:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.customerssuck.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customerssuck.com</A>  has a similar looking posting system, except they have a link on each topic where you can jump to your first unread post. Can you do that here?||||reg||1
Z||000033||LZeitgeist||07-09-2001||11:38 AM||||Cliff - some other boards (like EZBoards) have a 'Preview' feature that lets you see your post (with all the codes applied) *before* it gets sent to the board... this allows posters to check and make sure that all their photos and text codes and stuff work right before is gets sent in... <P>The 'Preview' feature on those boards is a selection at the bottom of the window, just like 'Submit Now', 'Spell Check' and 'Clear Fields', so that if someone is sending in a simple text-only post, they can just go ahead and send it without having to go through the 'Preview' screen, but it's a nice option for people who like to post pics and links and dress up their posts with smilies and colors and stuff...<P>Also, on the EZBoards, the "This post edited by..." message at the bottom of the posts is very small - noticeable, but smaller then the regular text... it still works, but it doesn't detract from the rest of the post that way... might you try that, too?<P>These are just suggestions of features that seem to be very useful elsewhere, since you seem to be in a mood to play around a bit, I thought you might like to try them... I have no idea what it would take to add those things, but I just thought I'd offer the ideas... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Keep up the great work, and thanks again for this place. <p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
